  "content": "Photosynthesis turns light into chemical energy in the chloroplasts. The light-dependent reactions in the thylakoid membranes produce ATP and NADPH. The Calvin cycle in the stroma uses them to fix carbon dioxide into glucose. Oxygen is released when water is split."
